{"id":"ram","name":"Ram","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:ram"],"groups":["4. A sheep"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ram","text":"Exalted. (1.) The son of Hezron, and one of the ancestors of the royal line (Ruth 4:19). The margin of 1 Chr. 2:9, also Matt. 1:3, 4 and Luke 3:33, have “Aram.” (2.) One of the sons of Jerahmeel (1 Chr. 2:25, 27). (3.) A person mentioned in Job 32:2 as founder of a clan to which Elihu belonged. The same as Aram of Gen. 22:21."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7410","lemma":"רָם","xlit":"Râm","gloss":"Ram, the name of an Arabian and of an Israelite","kjv":"Ram. See also H1027","count":6,"share":0.46},{"strong":"G689","lemma":"Ἀράμ","xlit":"Arám","gloss":"Aram , an Israelite","kjv":"Aram","count":3,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H3396","lemma":"יְרַחְמְאֵל","xlit":"Yᵉrachmᵉʼêl","gloss":"Jerachmeel, the name of three Israelites","kjv":"Jerahmeel","count":3,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H2696","lemma":"חֶצְרוֹן","xlit":"Chetsrôwn","gloss":"Chetsron, the name of a place in Palestine","kjv":"Hezron","count":3,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H352","lemma":"אַיִל","xlit":"ʼayil","gloss":"strength","kjv":"mighty, lintel, oak, post","count":4,"share":0.31},{"strong":"G5329","lemma":"Φάρες","xlit":"Pháres","gloss":"Phares , an Israelite","kjv":"Phares","count":2,"share":0.15}],"verses":["Ruth.4.19","1Chr.2.9","1Chr.2.10","1Chr.2.25","1Chr.2.27","Job.32.2","Exod.26.14","Exod.39.34","Dan.8.3","Dan.8.20","Matt.1.3","Matt.1.4","Luke.3.33"],"related":[{"id":"offerings","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"trumpets","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"amminadab","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.19,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"genealogies","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.055,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"genealogy","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.026,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"human-natur